          %h2#Motivation Motivation
          %p
            The central motivation for the study of a higher generalization of ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
            is the interest in extending the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            for a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the higher connected covers of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            through the whole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
            from Lie groups to such smooth
            = succeed "-groups." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %em fractional
            differential characteristic classes, that capture finer cohomological information.
          %h3#fractional_differential_classes Fractional differential classes
          %p
            We give some examples of such
            %em fractional characteristic classes
            that occur in practice.
          %p
            It is a familiar classical fact that the first
