          %p This kind of refinement we discuss in a bit more detail in the next section.
          %h3#higher_differential_spin_structures Higher differential spin structures
          %p
            These refined differential invariants of fractional characteristic classes are relevant in the discussion of higher differential spin structures. (See the first part of (
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#SSSII"} SatiSchreiberStasheff II
            for a review).) Ordinary
            = succeed "s" do
