                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{H}_{conn}(X,\mathbf{B}String)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\frac{1}{6}\hat p_2}{\to}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^7 U(1))
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In terms of the underlying
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#SSSIII"} SSSIII
          %p (…)
          %h3#chernsimons_theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            The refined higher Chern-Weil homomorphism takes values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            over
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+infinity-bundle"} connection on an infinity-bundle
            to this holonomy is a generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Therefore the higher Chern-Weil homomorphism defines a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            that we call
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"}> infinity-Chern-Simons theory
            \.
          %p See there for more details.
          %p Special noteworthy cases are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the class of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
                (
                %a{:href => "#FRS"}> FRS11
                )
            %li
              %p
                higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+supergravity"} Chern-Simons supergravity
              %p
                (see
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %strong ∞-Chern-Weil theory
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+models+and+general+theory"} Principal ∞-bundles – models and general theory
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+differential+structures"} Twisted differential structures
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Differential+String+and+Fivebrane+Structures"} Twisted Differential String and Fivebrane Structures
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Chern-Weil+Derivation+of+AKSZ+Sigma-Models"} Higher Chern-Weil Derivation of AKSZ Sigma-Models
          %h2#references References
          %p
            An explicit presentation of the
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            and the application to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+fivebrane+structure"} differential fivebrane structure
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} Cech Cocycles for Differential characteristic Classes
          %p
            The special case that gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-model"} AKSZ sigma-model
            is discussed in
          %ul#FRS
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
          %p A general abstract account is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p For a commented list of related literature see
          %p
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references"} differential cohomology in cohesive topos – references
